# World 2's ship deck and winch (SPEC 11, "World 2, slice 2", slice C). Ctrl+L, W, 5 starts mission 5 at the base pad; skill 1 is pinned after the
# world has loaded (no wind and no jets on skill 1, so the flight is the same every time) and ghost mode is on.
# The chopper flies out to the moored cargo ship (x 1730-1853, in the sea gap between the second and third island), settles into the 24 x 20 px
# hover box above its flat deck (x 1777-1800, skids 207-227): the hook falls, the rope hangs, a person climbs it and comes aboard (the first
# one 12 + 50 frames after the hover began, then one every 50 frames: 8 people in 8 s); the lamps are yellow in the box. Leaving the box pauses
# the climb. The card shows the ship on the strip map in place of a hut. The unit tests (testW2Deck*, testW2Winch*) hold the rules.
wait-serial "AGK t0" 1000
key 0x63
key 0x28
wait 5
key 0x11
wait 5
key 0x05
wait-serial "AGK world 2 loaded" 700
key 0x63
key 0x28
wait 5
key 0x01
wait 30
screenshot card
# the strip map: the ship (a blue hull on the sea, x 128-134, rows 128-129) in place of the third hut
expect-color card 131 129 0x36B
key 0x63
key 0x28
wait 5
key 0x24
wait 30
press fire 2
wait 60
press up 60
press left 771
press down 45
wait 30
wait-serial "AGK winch start" 300
wait 8
screenshot hook
wait 14
screenshot rope
# the moored ship's blue plating, under the hovering chopper
expect-color rope 170 240 0x36B near 4
wait-serial "AGK winch board=1" 200
wait 2
screenshot board1
wait-serial "AGK winch board=2" 200
wait 10
screenshot board2
press right 30
wait 10
screenshot away
expect-serial "AGK winch start[\s\S]*AGK winch board=1[\s\S]*AGK winch board=2"
expect-no-serial "AGK ERR|missing"
expect-no-dropped-frames
expect-max-load 90
expect-min-chip-free 96
